Regenerating the parsers with the registry's bison 3.8 and flex 2.6.4 (the
bison() and flex() targets of BUILD.bazel, in place of the checked-in bison
2.7 / flex 2.5 output in bisonflex/) needs one edit to the sources.

parser/bif.y gives INT_HASH and int_hash the tag <inthash_t>, which is not a
member of the grammar's %union.  Bison 2.7 never emitted code for the tag;
bison 3.8 emits the typed default action of `int_hash: INT_HASH` and the
compile fails with "union has no member named inthash_t".  The scanner never
produces INT_HASH and the only rule using int_hash logs that the attribute is
unsupported, so the two symbols are made untyped.

The scanner headers' `#include "FlexLexer.h"` already resolves, through the
include path, to the FlexLexer.h of the flex that generated the scanners
(@flex//:headers), so they need no edit.

diff -ruN a/parser/bif.y b/parser/bif.y
--- a/parser/bif.y	2026-10-28 16:53:33.505792743 -0700
+++ b/parser/bif.y	2026-10-28 16:53:33.516074562 -0700
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
 %token <core_t>         CORE
 %token <bhrsa_t>        BH_RSA
 %token <authhash_t>     AUTH_HASH
-%token <inthash_t>      INT_HASH
+%token      INT_HASH
 %token <pufhdloc_t>     PUFHD_LOC
 %token <optkey_t>       OPT_KEY
 %token <authonly_t>     AUTH_ONLY
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@
 %type <core_t>          core
 %type <bhrsa_t>         bh_rsa
 %type <authhash_t>      auth_hash
-%type <inthash_t>       int_hash
+%type       int_hash
 %type <pufhdloc_t>      pufhd_loc
 %type <optkey_t>        opt_key
 %type <authonly_t>      auth_only
